        <section id="what-is-data?"  class="t-bg-primary">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          What is Data?
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>In computing Data is information that has been translated into a form that can be read, moved and processed by the computer. Data is any collection of numbers, characters or other symbols that have been coded into a format that can be inputted into a computer and processed. On its own data means nothing but after processing it becomes information.  The main types of data that can be inputted into a computer are numeric, text, dates, graphics and sound. Raw data is a term used to describe data in its most basic digital form.</p>
<p>Data is digitally written, stored, and read on physical units such as CPUs, hard drives, and RAM. Data is stored by electrical circuits on the disk which are defined by binary inputs. To create these circuits, transistors within the processing units determine which binary state (on, ‘1’s or off, ‘0’s) parts of the memory are in.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/uc/uc_u2_s1_p3_image.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
     
    
  
  
