        <section id="what-is-the-purpose-of-data-types-in-coding?"  class="t-bg-primary">
          
            <h2>What is the purpose of data types in coding?</h2>
              <p>Data types in computing vary and can come in all shapes and sizes. Some are used to store numbers, some are used for text and some for more complicated types of data. A data type tells a computer system how to interpret its value.</p>
<p>Let's have a look at some of the common data types.</p>

              
              
<div class="gallery-container">
  <div role="group" class="gallery no-js">
    <ul>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Integer (int)
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>This is the most common numeric data type used to store whole numbers without fractions. Some examples of int’s are: 1, 0, -5, 263</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/uc/uc_u2_s1_p3_slide1.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Float (or Real)
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>This is also a numeric data type used to store numbers that contain decimal points (like money) or for fractions. Float means ‘floating point’ number. Some examples of floats are: 0.3, 5.28568, -743.34854, 0.0</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/uc/uc_u2_s1_p3_slide2.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Character (char)
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>Is used to store a single letter, digit, punctuation mark, symbol or blank space. There are different types of blank spaces including a single space ‘ ‘, a new line character (known as a carriage), as well as tabs. Different characters specify upper/lower case characters. Some examples of chars are: y, T, !, 1</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/uc/uc_u2_s1_p3_slide3.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          String (str or text)
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>Is the most common data type used to store text. It is a sequence of characters that can appear on a keyboard such as letters, numbers and symbols. Strings can contain any combination of characters: upper case, lower case, numerals, and symbols. The limit of how long a string depends on the language. Some example of strings are: Dog, sALamI, jump!, 21*&amp;*(&quot;1</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/uc/uc_u2_s1_p3_slide4.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Boolean (bool)
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>It used where data is restricted to true/false or yes/no options, also using binary true (1) or false (0).  Examples of Boolean are: TRUE, FALSE or 1, 0</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/uc/uc_u2_s1_p3_slide5.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

            
          
